from parts/safari-enter.replay
# sys-safari-balls (docs/research/great-marsh.md): one Safari Ball left. Thrown at a Wooper: a miss ends the game in
# the battle ("You're out of Safari Balls! Game over!", the player's flight), the field comes back at the gate
# (the special location) and SAFARI_GAME 9 ends the game; a catch ends it in the field (SAFARI_GAME 2: the chime,
# "You've run out of Safari Balls", the warp). Either way the gate's on-frame script walks the player out.
set state safari {"balls":1,"steps":0,"caught":0}
+0 press up
until position 68 112
+0 release up
until idle
+0 press right
until position 74 112
+0 release right
until idle
+0 press up
until position 74 109
+0 release up
until idle 900
until wild platinum:SPECIES_WOOPER up down 20000
battle catch platinum:ITEM_SAFARI_BALL 30000
# After a catch the field's "run out of Safari Balls" waits for A without an arrow (wait_ab_press).
+120 press a
+1 release a
+120 press a
+1 release a
until idle 3000
